# Keeps two things that are not part of the site from being served, on a host that reads
# .htaccess (Apache): a `.git` folder, when the site is put in place with `git clone` or
# `git pull`, and this folder's README.md, which is written for the person who hosts it.
# If every page answers 500 after an upload, the host does not allow these lines: delete
# this file, and keep `.git` and README.md out of the web folder by hand instead.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/\.git
RedirectMatch 404 ^/README\.md$
